From f391fa8256f78e4a31a0db952d0c75abd0c8f46e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "kevin.krausse" <kkrausse97@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 09:12:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/21] ggml-webgpu: exact buffer accounting, grow-only pooled
 compute buffer in size classes, one param write per batch

Accounting (ggml_backend_webgpu_stats_json): every buffer goes through
ggml_webgpu_create_buffer / ggml_webgpu_destroy_buffer, so live bytes and
counts are exact for the backend, split by purpose (weights, compute, kept
compute, staging, params) with weight bytes by tensor type, plus cumulative
counts of buffers created and destroyed, pipelines, bind group layouts, bind
groups, command encoders, submits, queue writes and maps.

Pool: the previous cache reused a freed compute buffer only when it was at most
2x + 16 MiB larger than the request and otherwise destroyed everything kept and
made a buffer of the exact size. In live transcription every run has a
different length, mostly a little longer than the one before, so most runs
destroyed one buffer and created another (60 s of fake-microphone live use: 108
buffers created and destroyed over 202 runs; 300 random lengths: 92). Now a
freed compute buffer is kept, an allocation takes the smallest kept buffer that
fits, and a new one is created in a size class (4 MiB steps to 16 MiB, then at
most 25% over), destroying the buffer it outgrew first. After the longest run
has been seen once no run creates a buffer. The read-back staging buffer grows
in powers of two from 1 MiB. GGML_WEBGPU_POOL=legacy restores the old policy
for comparison; GGML_WEBGPU_BUFFER_CACHE=0 still turns pooling off.

Per run, fewer objects for the browser to collect: uniform parameters are
staged on the CPU and written once per submitted batch (54 queue writes per
110m encoder run instead of about 1100), and a pipeline's bind group layout is
fetched once when the pipeline is made instead of once per dispatch
(getBindGroupLayout returns a new object each call). Bind groups are still one
per dispatch (1111 per 110m run): their offsets and sizes change with the
length.

Text unchanged on a07/a14/a56 for 110m Q8_0 and Q4_0 (native and Chrome).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
